Revision 5.3 addresses the earlier residual and interval-property defects, and explicitly gates the disputed ending path. I’ve also found a separate issue in the storage fix: tagging an old object `ended` does not restart S3’s object-age clock, so it could still be deleted before the promised post-end retention period. I’m checking the liveness bounds and the exact scope of the gate before giving the verdict.
