docs/V1-SERVICE-RESOLUTIONS.md:24:| S5 request lifecycle | The client supplies a **request key** (a UUID). The same key returns the same request and the same receipt, every time. The same content under a different key is a separate request with its own receipt. States: ACCEPTED, COMPLETE, REFUSED, FAILED. Acceptance is durable once the ACCEPTED response is sent. Only the client credential that made a request may look it up or retrieve it. No cancellation in V1. Lookup and identical-result retrieval last **30 days** after the request ends (COMPLETE, REFUSED or FAILED). After that, lookup returns EXPIRED. A content-free record of the key is kept until issuance closes, so an expired key cannot start a new issuance. | Owner |
docs/V1-SERVICE-RESOLUTIONS.md:25:| S6 content exposure | Requests and results are readable only by the submitting client credential. Transport is encrypted. Refused content is not stored. Content and results are deleted 30 days after the request ends, copies included. Content is used for nothing but the request. A receipt the client hands to others exposes the content to them: that is the client's choice. | Owner |
docs/V1-SERVICE-RESOLUTIONS.md:34:| AJ5 exit | **AUTHOR.** Recommendation: for a planned shutdown, 30 days' public notice, and archiving the authority records and git repository with an independent archive (for example Zenodo). A final verifier release only if release authorization is still trustworthy (profile §15.9 R5 stops new releases after a release-key compromise). For an unexpected shutdown: notice and archiving as far as practicable. | Author |
docs/V1-SERVICE-RESOLUTIONS.md:42:| L1 window dates and closure | Both window endpoints are fixed and published before issuance preparation, at most 90 days apart. The actual dates stay OPEN until the dated operating record; a late first issuance does not extend the window. Signing stops 96 hours before the window ends (the runbook's operating margin, not a registered rule). Acceptance stops 120 hours before the end, so that every accepted request can complete or fail (S4) before signing stops. Only receipts that pass the registered window checks are shipped. Completed results stay retrievable for 30 days (S5). Closure is announced 14 days ahead on the service page. | Owner |
